{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "05", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "40", "S": "28"}}, "news": [{"title": "Government to complete statewide land resurvey by next year: Telangana revenue minister", "para": "Telangana is set to complete a comprehensive resurvey of all land parcels by next year. This initiative aims to provide legally secure land records to landowners and farmers. Officials will ensure transparency throughout the survey process, while farmers' presence will be mandatory during field operations. Regular oversight will be conducted by officials at various levels to monitor the program's progress.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/government-to-complete-statewide-land-resurvey-by-next-year-telangana-revenue-minister/135564402?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-379330/135564402.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Telangana government expands Indiramma Towers housing project to four more cities", "para": "The Telangana government has announced the development of the Indiramma Towers across four cities: Nizamabad, Warangal, Nalgonda, and Karimnagar. Designed to cater to low-income families, these towers will feature one ground floor and five additional levels. The initial phase allocates 4.5 lakh homes, with construction currently underway for 1.9 lakh units and plans for an extra 2.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/telangana-government-expands-indiramma-towers-housing-project-to-four-more-cities/135564257?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-303442/135564257.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Max Estates\u2019 net profit declines 40% to \u20b94.67 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "Max Estates faced a significant downturn, with a net consolidated profit drop of 40.2 percent for Q2 FY27. However, the company thrived in pre-sales, achieving \u20b92,092 crore, almost doubling its collections to \u20b9560 crore over the prior year. Furthermore, the firm has initiated memoranda of understanding for project launches in Ghaziabad and West Delhi, showcasing its commitment to expand its development portfolio, even amid profit challenges.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/max-estates-net-profit-declines-40-to-4-67-crore-in-q2-fy27/135563824?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-26190/135563824.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}